## Test files written this session

- .worktrees/recurring-tasks/test/series.test.ts (CREATE) — new file; no prior version existed. Covers PRD AC-11..AC-18 (plan AC-A1..AC-A8) against `/api/series`'s planned four endpoints (`POST /`, `GET /`, `GET /:id`, `PATCH /:id`) and migration 0005's `recurrence_series_priority_chk` CHECK, none of which exist yet (test-first).

  Confirmed RED for the right reasons — ran `npx prettier --write test/series.test.ts` (no changes; already conformant) then `npx vitest run test/series.test.ts` inside the worktree: **18 failed / 4 passed (22 total)**, zero transform/import/syntax errors.
  - 13 failures are direct `404` (or a `200`-vs-`404` on the list read) where `201`/`400`/`200` was expected — every `/api/series` request currently falls through to Hono's `app.notFound`, because `src/worker/routes/series.ts` does not exist and no route is mounted (plan Tasks 5-7).
  - 4 failures (`AC-17` ×2, `AC-18` ×2) are `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined` — a direct cascade of the same 404: the test destructures `{ series }` from a `POST /api/series` response body that is actually `{ error: "Not found" }`, so `series` is `undefined` and the next line's property read throws. Same root cause, not an independent defect.
  - 1 failure is the AC-14 direct-DB-insert case: `db.insert(recurrenceSeries).values({ priority: "urgent" as any, ... })` was expected to reject and instead resolved successfully — `recurrence_series_priority_chk` does not exist yet because migration 0005 has not been generated/applied (plan Tasks 1-2).
  - The 4 PASSING tests are `describe("AC-15 / AC-A5 Token gate")`'s four no-token cases (`GET /`, `POST /`, `GET /:id`, `PATCH /:id` all return `401`): these pass **legitimately**, not by accident — `app.use("/api/*", requireToken)` in `src/worker/index.ts` runs ahead of route dispatch, so the auth gate already rejects an unauthenticated request before Hono ever needs a matching route. This is exactly the plan's own claim ("`/api/series` inherits the token gate for free", Task 7's `# SOURCE` note) and is why AC-15 is green before any of Tasks 1-7 land.

  No other RED reason was observed (no compile error, no unresolved import, no assertion bug in the test file itself).

